% spec: §6.3.4 step 2 an 'if' or 'do' skipped while recovering is abandoned too: its 'else' or 'while (...) ;' tail is skipped, not reported.
while (x +) if (y) a; else b;
if (x +) if (y) a; else b; else c;
if (x) a b; else if (c) d; else e;
while (x +) do a; while (b);
while (x +) if (y) a; else b; else c;
